---
import { TextSection } from '@components/odyssey-theme';
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Page.astro';

const seo = {
  title: 'Terms of use | tevsys',
  description:
    'tevsys terms of use: MT5 utility, monitoring scope, market execution, HyperClose, evidence and liability limits.',
};
---

<Layout seo={seo} lang="en">
  <TextSection narrow>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>

    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      This document sets out the general terms of use of the tevsys.io website and the tevsys™ product
      (utility / Expert Advisor for MetaTrader 5). It complements the operational description on
      <a href="/en/como-funciona">How it works</a> (including
      <a href="/en/como-funciona#vigilancia-vps">Monitoring: what tevsys covers — and what it does not</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>Nature of the product</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      tevsys is a <strong>local utility</strong> for risk management and operational discipline. It enforces
      the limits and rules <strong>you</strong> configure (daily and/or weekly loss and gain limits, OFF days,
      lock when a limit is reached, and optional layers by plan). It executes automatic closes according to
      that agreement.
    </p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      It does <strong>not</strong> trade on the user’s behalf, does <strong>not</strong> issue trading
      signals, does <strong>not</strong> manage buy/sell strategies, does <strong>not</strong> custody funds
      and does <strong>not</strong> constitute financial, investment or trading advice.
    </p>

    <h2>User responsibility</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      The user is solely responsible for configuring their limits, for their trading decisions and for the
      results of using the product. tevsys enforces what the user configures; the decision is always theirs.
      The execution environment (MetaTrader 5, broker, network, VPS or computer) is the user’s
      responsibility.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope of monitoring</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      Tick-by-tick monitoring (evaluating limits and sending closes) only exists while MetaTrader 5 and
      tevsys are running on a machine with market access (home PC or VPS). That is not a hidden product
      failure: it is how a program that runs inside the terminal works.
    </p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      If MetaTrader is closed, the machine is powered off with no other active terminal, or tevsys is
      removed from the chart, live monitoring is <strong>paused</strong>. The agreement state (limits, lock,
      protection snapshot) may remain stored; when you reload, tevsys reattaches with those same percentages —
      not as a fake “free” panel. Detail and panel wording:
      <a href="/en/como-funciona#vigilancia-vps">monitoring and gaps</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Market execution</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      When a configured limit is reached, tevsys <strong>processes and sends</strong> the close order to the
      broker through MetaTrader 5. The final fill price and outcome are determined by the market and the
      broker (slippage, spread, liquidity, gaps, first tick when quoting resumes, network latency).
    </p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      tevsys cannot force an exact price on market orders. Where the product documents it, the record
      separates the <strong>tevsys decision</strong> (limit trigger) from <strong>MT5 execution</strong>.
      Published precision figures (e.g. average error under normal conditions) are not a guarantee of outcome
      on every trade; extreme cases are documented separately.
    </p>

    <h2>HyperClose and trading while locked</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      If, with active protection or on an OFF day as configured, the user tries to open new trades,
      HyperClose may immediately close that new exposure and log the attempt. Insisting on trading while
      locked means accepting the cost and risk of those attempts. MetaTrader stays open: tevsys does not
      “turn off” the terminal.
    </p>

    <h2>Evidence and records</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      tevsys may generate logs and records that can be checked against official MetaTrader 5 reports for the
      same period. That evidence helps verify compliance and event sequence; it is <strong>not</strong> a
      broker-audit service, a profit guarantee, or a legal/regulatory opinion.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, tevsys™ and its rights holders are not liable for loss or
      damage arising from: broker or network slippage or delays; market gaps; MetaTrader 5, VPS or broker
      server outages, updates or shutdowns; use without active monitoring (gaps with no terminal); incorrect
      limit configuration by the user; or insisting on trading while locked.
    </p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      Unless mandatory law provides otherwise, any financial liability related to use of the software is
      limited, at most, to the amount paid for the licence in the relevant period. This clause will be
      reviewed and formalized with professional legal advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of content</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      All content published on this website (texts, videos, screenshots, reports, technical documentation)
      is the property of tevsys™ and is protected by intellectual property rights. Reproduction or
      distribution without express authorization is prohibited.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal review</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      These terms describe the product with operational honesty. They will be reviewed and formalized with
      professional legal advice (ownership details, GDPR, liability cap and jurisdiction). For any enquiry:
      <a href="mailto:info@tevsys.io">info@tevsys.io</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="legal-update">Last updated: 26 September 2026</p>
  </TextSection>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-update {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
</style>
